, boring would be good. We could all use that right about now. \uc2 Jon Allen\uc2 , Stuart Stevens, thank you both for joining, always good to see you.\par \par \uc2 STEVENS: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: When we come back, just when you start to think it is time for the big finale, Serena update when the 11 Hour continues.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [23:58:25]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Serena Williams just supreme in the final set when she had to be.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: The last thing before we go tonight, the comeback Queen, the everything queen. You know, we could not end this program this evening without an update on Serena Williams and her historic US Open ran. The 40- year-old tennis legend continued her winning streak and her career tonight, beating the second ranked tennis player in the world in a hard fought three set battle. Celebrities packed the stands yet again this evening for the Serena show, including another queen in her own right, you just saw her on the screen, the great Dionne Warwick and if she was saying a little prayer for Serena, it definitely worked. Here`s what Serena had to say about her career extended.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DIONNE WARWICK: You are taking your time evolving away from tennis. What do you say about that?\par \par \uc2 SERENA WILLIAMS: You know, it`s no rush here. I`m just -- I`m loving this crowd -- oh my goodness, it`s really fantastic. So, there`s still a little left in me, we`ll see the neck. We`ll see.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: I don`t think I`ve ever seen Tiger Woods smile that big. And I would say there`s more than a little left in Serena. And while we anxiously await round three, we can all catch Serena playing doubles tomorrow night. with her sister Venus and after that we will see you right here at 11.\par \par \uc2 [00:00:04]\par \par \uc2 And on that note, we wish you all a very good night. From all of our colleagues across the networks and NBC News, thanks for staying up late with us. I`ll see you at the end of tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 THIS IS A RUSH TRANSCRIPT. THIS COPY MAY NOT BE IN ITS FINAL FORM AND MAY BE UPDATED. END\par \par \uc2 Content and programming copyright 2022 MSNBC.  ALL RIGHTS  RESERVED.  Copyright 2022 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All materials herein are  protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced,  distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the  prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You may not alter  or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the  content. \par \par \uc2 Document BRIWIL0020220901ei8v00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 CHRIS JANSING REPORTS for August 30, 2022, MSNBC\b0\par\par\uc2 Andrea Mitchell, Courtney Kube, Josh Lederman, Erin McLaughlin,  Jake Ward, Mike Memoli, Sahil Kapur, Eugene Daniels, Ryan Reilly, Tom  Winter \par \uc2 7,780 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2022\par \uc2 MSNBC: Meet the Press Daily\par \uc2 MSNMPD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 CQ-Roll Call, Inc. All rights reserved. Prepared by CQ-Roll Call, Inc. \par \par \uc2 [13:00:00]\par \par \uc2 ANDREA MITCHELL, MSNBC ANCHOR: Good afternoon, I am Andrea Mitchell in for Chris Jansing.\par \par \uc2 President Biden, returning to what works for him in 2020, Pennsylvania, and the battle for the soul of America. Just a few hours, the president is set to speak about crime in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, kicking off the first of three trips to the state this week, critical to defeating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2020. In that speech today, he is going to be playing offense pushing back on MAGA Republicans, who have called for defunding the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , calling that a threat to our rule of law, and pointing to the White House funding the hiring of 100,000 police. And drawing on the -- also the contrast that he`s been trying to paint between Democrats and that wing of the Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 It`s a contrast that the president will be taking to primetime on Thursday with a speech in front of Independence Hall, the theme, The Battle For The Soul Of The Nation, of course, the theme with which he kicked off his 2020 campaign. A message he hopes resonates with voters just 10 weeks away from the midterms as Democrats begin to gain momentum trying to shut down Republican hopes of a red wave this fall.\par \par \uc2 Joining us now is NBC News White House correspondent Mike Memoli from Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, NBC News senior national political reporter Sahil Kapur, Politico White House reporter and playbook co-author Eugene Daniels, and Philadelphia Inquirer Political Reporter Julia Terruso. So, Mike, Scranton Joe is back in Pennsylvania near Scranton Wilkes-Barre, close enough with a special primetime address later this week. What do we expect to hear from him today, Thursday night, and, of course, the Labor Day parade in Pittsburgh, which is my annual opportunity to watch Mike Memoli trying to run as fast as he can dodging the Secret Service agents and, of course, the president was talking to him because that`s what he does, Mike?\par \par \uc2 MIKE MEMOLI, MSNBC WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT: It might -- it might be a little harder this year, Andrea, but I did bring my running shoes last. We`re on the road with President Biden, as you can hear the Marine Corps Band also here in Pennsylvania with the president today. Now, we`ve been talking for some time, Andrea, about the fact that White House advisors really do want to get the president back out on the road.\par \par \uc2 And now with 10 weeks to go until the midterm elections, we finally are seeing the president ramp up his engagement in the midterm conversation. Maybe not necessarily appearing with down-ballot Democrats all over the country, but doing what a president uniquely can do, which is set the conversation really dictate the terms of the conversation.\par \par \uc2 And we`re seeing the president do that in earnest this week. Four stops with three of them here in Pennsylvania alone and the biggest platform that any president has a prime time address with that historic backdrop you mentioned, Independence Hall. I was talking recently with one of Biden`s closest advisors and he said there`s really two tracks that they`re focused on with the midterm messaging.\par \par \uc2 The first, this is a president, you know, Andrea, who prides himself on understanding that connection to middle-class voters. The concerns about the economy, inflation, obviously are going to be a major part of the conversation this year. And the president thinks he has a case to make with some of his legislative accomplishments, especially recently on that score.\par \par \uc2 But the reemergence or maybe the persistence in the presence of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  looming over the Republican Party really has given this White House - - this president the opportunity to return to what they think was that winning message in 2020, but also in the 2018 midterm elections, to really frame this as an election in which our very rights, especially in the wake of that Supreme Court decision are at stake in this election. So the president going to be making that argument that we are in a continued battle for the soul of the -- of America, and that he`s going to make it clear as a White House official said, who is fighting for our rights, our democracy, our freedoms, and who is not.\par \par \uc2 And to further illustrate really the gift that some Biden advisors feel Donald Trump`s presence is giving to this party to illustrate that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself is going to be in this very region of Pennsylvania over the weekend, appearing with \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , of course, the gubernatorial nominee on the Republican side who himself has been a sort of partaking in the same kind of what Biden would call MAGA extremism. It`s really helped Democrats do what they want to do when you`re in the party in power, making this a choice election rather than a referendum election, Andrea.\par \par \uc2 MITCHELL: And in particular, Mastriano on the abortion issue and the democracy issues since he led the "Stop The Steal" movement in Pennsylvania to stop certifying Joe Biden`s victory there. Apparently, the president spoke, I guess, on his way to Andrews Air Force Base.\par \par \uc2 Let me get that clear. OK, OK. Sorry, he didn`t speak. He`s on his way to Marine One where he`s going to be taking off. I think we just showed you that picture. He`s going to be taken off shortly when he arrives on Marine One, boards Air Force One and then, of course, goes to Wilkes-Barre where Mike Memoli is.\par \par \uc2 Eugene Daniels, so let`s talk about this. We`re 10 weeks away from the midterms. Top issue is the threat to democracy and certainly that messaging could, they hope -- the Democrats hope galvanized people to vote.\par \par \uc2 [13:05:00]\par \par \uc2 So far, that has not been that important a political message for Democrats, and they certainly didn`t get any legislation through to the disappointment of a lot of progressives.\par \par \uc2 EUGENE DANIELS, WHITE HOUSE REPORTER, POLITICO: That`s absolutely right. They have been talking about voting rights, for example, for a long time trying to get something done there. They were unable to do so obviously because of the filibuster in the Senate. But just recently, in an NBC News poll, for the first time, we saw that threat to democracy overtook even concerns about the economy for some voters. That`s one poll, obviously. But that is something that for Democrats, especially this White House, who are hoping to make this as Mike just said, choice election as opposed to a referendum election, that this is something that they`re going to be able to glom on to.\par \par \uc2 It is the reason why President Biden joined the race for president