tting that towline, but the Iranians cut it first. So we got a statement, a brief statement from the head of U.S. Central Command, General Michael Eric Kurilla. He praised the U.S. professionalism in this case saying that, "The professionalism and competence of the crew of the USS Thunderbolt prevented Iran from this illegal action."\par \par \uc2 This incident once again demonstrates Iran`s continued destabilizing, illegal, and unprofessional activity in the Middle East. The U.S. Military maintaining that they were in international waters at the time and that this incident, which lasted four hours, that ended because of the result of the professionalism of the \uc2 U.S. Navy\uc2  in this instance.\par \par \uc2 MITCHELL: A close call. Courtney Kube, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 And the White House has just announced that the \uc2 USAID\uc2  will give another $30 million in humanitarian assistance to Pakistan responding of course to the deadly flooding there. More than a third of Pakistan is under water. A monster monsoon devastating the country. More than a thousand people have reportedly been killed. Now actually 1100 people, displacing half a million more, causing billions in damages.\par \par \uc2 Today the \uc2 U.N\uc2 . Secretary General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2  called it a monsoon on steroids. He called for emergency aid for the country. Experts believe this monster monsoon is the result of human-made climate change.\par \par \uc2 And coming up, broken promises. A year after fleeing Afghanistan to start a new life, some of those who left everything behind are raising concerns about what they found here in America. That report coming up.\par \par \uc2 You`re watching CHRIS JANSING REPORTS only on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:36:46]\par \par \uc2 MITCHELL: And moments ago, Ukraine`s President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  announced that U.S. Senators Rob Portman and Amy Klobuchar are in Ukraine right now coming the same day 