ation keeps making things look worse for Trump. Then --\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, HOST, \uc2 FOX\uc2  NEWS: President Trump`s legal team requested the appointment of a special master.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You know, this is kind of a last resort situation.\par \par \uc2 HAYES: Why a Trump-appointed judge is scoffing at his attempt to slow down the investigation.\par \par \uc2 And if it`s election night, Steve Kornacki is here for all the results from New York, Florida, and beyond when ALL IN starts right now.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HAYES (on camera): Good evening from New York. I`m Chris Hayes. We do indeed have a lot going on tonight as you can see from the bottom of your screen there because it is an election night. We`ve got primary elections in three states, New York, Florida, and Oklahoma. Now, polls have just closed in Florida and Oklahoma. There`ll be closing in New York at 9:00 p.m. New Yorkers, if you`re watching this, you still have an hour to vote.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, I can tell you now that NBC News projects former governor and current Congressman \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  who`s had a pretty remarkable career as the projected winner of the Democratic primary for governor, defeating Florida Commissioner of Agriculture \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 . She`s the only statewide Democrat in that state. He will then be running against \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , for his old job as governor of Florida.\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman Val Demings is the projected winner of the Democratic primary for Senate. She will face off in a marquee Senate race with Republican Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  in November. We`re going to bring you some more updates. Of course, the great Steve Kornacki will be here to take us through all the races to watch in just a little bit.\par \par \uc2 But the news continues to break two weeks now since the \uc2 FBI\uc2  searched on Trump`s home at Mar-a-Lago with every new revelation every