f war, a different kind of military combat than we have seen. It is so focused on terror (ph) civilian. It fits the actual legal definition in the United States law of how we define terrorist acts of coercion and intimidation with violence against the civilian population to achieve political ends.\par \par \uc2 And so I think there are a whole set of issues and legal issues that unfold at this state designation of terrorism. We need to start with calling a spade a spade and here, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , the Russia regime is using terror against the Ukrainian people and we shouldn`t shy away from speaking plainly and clearly about that.\par \par \uc2 CAPEHART: And one last question for you, Damon, real quickly, you visited Ukraine in May. As Russia`s war in Ukraine enters its fifth month, what does support for Ukraine look like these days?\par \par \uc2 WILSON: You know, it`s really remarkable. When you`re still traveling across the United States, seeing Ukrainian flags. We`ve seen opinion polls in Germany showing really strong support for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The support is not just support for military weapons but is support for the humanitarian, it`s support for Ukrainian civil society as to empower the Ukrainian people to really shape their own destiny here.\par \par \uc2 And I think right now there is a real focus among our partners in thinking about how do we build not just what was in Ukraine but how to rebuild a future Ukraine that is a stronger democracy. And that will ultimately be a victory over Putin.\par \par \uc2 CAPEHART: Damon Wilson, thank you very much for joining us tonight.\par \par \uc2 That is tonight`s LAST WORD. I will see you this weekend on "THE SUNDAY SHOW" starting at 10:00 a.m. Eastern here on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 [22:59:53]\par \par \uc2 Much more on the breaking January 6th news on the Secret Service subpoena on "THE 11TH HOUR WITH STEPHANIE RUHLE" which starts right now.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RUHLE, MSNBC HOST: Tonight, breaking 