en the president kind of, you know, really fall behind in his response to abortion. Failed to adequately respond to things like critical race theory. And not aggressively take on the Republicans in a way that I think Democrats see fit. You know, when he calls \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  a person of honor, I think a lot of Democrats are kind of left scratching their heads wondering, you know, if \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  is a person of honor, then, you know, what are we doing here?\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Michael Starr Hopkins, Ian Calderon, great conversation, guys. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 More questions and no clear answers. How the families of the Uvalde victims are grappling with the new video of the shooting and what`s next for that grieving community.\par \par \uc2 You`re watching CHRIS JANSING REPORTS only on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [13:53:12]\par \par \uc2 JANSING: Today we`re hearing raw emotion and palpable frustration from the families of victims killed in the Uvalde school shooting as they process the leaked video from inside the school.\par \par \uc2 NBC`s Antonia Hylton joins me now from Uvalde where she has been speaking with those families.\par \par \uc2 Antonia, the unspeakable heartbreak seems to have only been exacerbated by what we`ve seen what they have experienced over the past couple of days. What are you hearing?\par \par \uc2 ANTONIA HYLTON, NBC NEWS CORRESPONDENT: Well, that`s exactly right, Chris. It`s unspeakable. And for many people the release of this video has come like an utter gut punch. And, you know, people knew that over an hour went by before cops confronted the gunman so they had a sense of what they might see when this footage finally became available to families and the community.\par \par \uc2 But there`s nothing like really seeing all of this unfold. And in particular I think it`s hard to see those moments when the police retreat, for example, to see the young boy who spots the shooter and 