MERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [17:29:25]\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: Welcome back to POLITICSNATION.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now to provide their insights into today`s biggest topics is my political panel, Sarah Longwell, Director for Republicans for the Rule of Law and Publisher of opinion website, "The Bulwark" and Danielle Moody, host of "Woke AF Podcast" and cohost of "Democracy-ish."\par \par \uc2 Sarah, the next January 6 Committee hearing is set for this Tuesday. The Committee was zero in on the participation of White nationalist groups that comprised the January 6 mob and their connection to the Trump White House.\par \par \uc2 [17:30:11]\par \par \uc2 SHARPTON: Now, this follows key witness testimony from Trump`s former White House Counsel who sat down for a whopping seven and a half hour interview Friday.\par \par \uc2 What impact do you think these proceedings are having going into the midterms?\par \par \uc2 SARAH LONGWELL, DIRECTOR, REPUBLICANS FOR THE RULE OF LAW: Well, these hearings have completely exceeded expectations, in terms of you know, we sat for two impeachment hearings that really went nowhere, but we are getting a lot of information about what Trump did. In terms of, you know, the impact going into the midterms that I`m not sure about, but I do think that they`re having a big impact on us learning the truth.\par \par \uc2 I mean, the fact that \uc2 Pat Cipollone\uc2 , you know, we`re going to learn what he testified to and he can confirm, you know, Cassidy Hutchinson`s explosive testimony that we heard now, going back two weeks, we`re going to learn, you know, things were Trump was discussing, you know, maybe he got recommendations from Cipollone that he then went against and actually broke the law.\par \par \uc2 I mean, we heard so much from Cassidy Hutchinson that was just mind blowing. And if he is there, to confirm, then that`s going to be really meaningful.\par \par \uc2 I just want to make one last point on Cipollone. You know, he is not 