t the price you pay at the pump is very, very, very important. What you need to fill up your tank is an extremely important economic thing. But you talked about Ukraine, the President`s leadership on that was tremendous, putting that coalition together. And we have to sell the importance of that. And I realize that these are maybe complex issues, the relationship of inflation and the price of gas to Ukraine, but what else would we do? What else could we done --\par \par \uc2 STEELE: Let me give you the complexities real quick cow going into the fall. Republican messaging are two points. One, the Democrats have ruined the economy. That`s why you`re paying high prices at the gas tank. And that`s why inflation --\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Well that point is not true.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: It doesn`t matter. And number two, number two, Republicans is that Democrats want to groom our kids. That`s that -- that touches on everything.\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: Also not true.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: We know that.\par \par \uc2 FRANKEN: Well that`s just incredibly offensive.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: (INAUDIBLE) for message.\par \par \uc2 FRANKEN: Yes. And I know you don`t believe it`s like. All I know you don`t believe that.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: No, I don`t believe that --\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: All right, gentlemen. Hold on. I`m not going to let either of you go anywhere. But we do have to take a quick break. We have more to cover on the other side. Stick around. We`re talking \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [23:48:27]\par \par \uc2 RUHLE: From political friends to possible foes, the rising influence of Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  within the GOP is a potential challenge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a potential complication for Democrats. So let`s get back with Al Franken and Michael Steele. All, Max Booth, columnist for the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  says DeSantis is an even greater threat to democracy than Trump. What do you think?\par \par \